# home-bateria-externa: the firmware's main screen with an external supply
# connected (13.8 V) and the battery at 12.1 V, charging. It is the same base as
# home-usb-20m; the only difference is the supply state that pushes the power
# clock past the firmware's 0..10 V battery mapping:
#   (uint8_t)(v_bat * 10) = (uint8_t)(12.1 * 10) = 121, which no case of the
#   `switch` in src/clock.c covers. It is the fixture that reproduces UI-009
#   (the power-clock battery symbol was an uninitialized pointer, so the first
#   glyph of the first line was memory, not a battery icon).
# At the accepted toolchain (Ubuntu 24.04) the base renders the garbage text
# "EHE 12.1v"; with another toolchain the same read is undefined (segfault).
#
# `charging true` tells the two lines apart from home-usb-20m: with the charger
# on, the second line's icon is SYMBOL_PLUG_CHARGE instead of SYMBOL_PLUG.

name home-bateria-externa
screen main

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging true

rxtx rx
